encyclopedia :pyre_afterheat do
  name "Pyre Afterheat"
  summary "Pyre afterheat is the flameless heat surge that follows a kinetic-band resonance event the way a struck bell's hum follows its strike note — arriving hours later, softening exposed seals and re-annealing glass along the Cinder Gap cordon. The cordon services time their inspections to it, and seal work in afterheat country is scheduled like tide work."
  kind :phenomenon
  subkind :catastrophe
  status :complete
  topics :resonance, :"kinetic-freq", :danger, :rebuilding
  prevalence :uncommon
  appears_when all: { place: [:cordon, :hot] }
  medium "Ground and structure along kinetic-band fault country — the Cinder Gap line above all; the surge travels the rock and the built fabric bolted to it"
  nature "A delayed thermal release following kinetic resonance events: the ground takes the event's energy as a struck bell takes a blow, and gives it back hours later as heat — the hum after the strike"
  hazard "The surge softens seal compounds, waxes, and low-grade gaskets across exposed faces; a cordon seal inspected before the afterheat and trusted after it is the region's classic false pass"
  known_forms "The single surge after a discrete event; the long warm week after a resonance storm; and the standing afterheat of the Gap's central reach, where events overlap and the ground rings warm year-round"

  descriptive_identity(
    signs: "Hours after the shake, exposed metal grows warm to the touch under still " \
           "air, seal wax glosses and slumps at the corners, and the survey strips " \
           "along the cordon line darken in the order the surge travels — the heat " \
           "walking the fault the way sound walks a rail.",
    effects: "Seal compounds soften and reset, glass surfaces re-anneal glossy, and " \
             "the cordon's instruments log a thermal wave moving at survey-clock " \
             "speed along the line, its strength tracking the event that fathered it.",
    hazards: "A seal that held at inspection can slump in the surge and set wrong — " \
             "the false pass — so afterheat law re-inspects everything the wave " \
             "touched, and the interval between event and surge is working time " \
             "spent battening, venting, and moving the soft stores."
  )

  prose <<~PROSE
    The Cinder Gap country receives resonance events in two stages. The kinetic-band shake comes first; hours later, the ground releases heat in a flameless surge that travels the fault line at survey-clock speed, warming exposed metal, slumping seal wax, and re-annealing glass faces. Cordon teaching compares the sequence to a struck bell and its continuing hum. The #{ref :cinder_gap, "Gap's"} instruments have charted event strength against surge strength and shake hour against surge hour for generations, and publish the ratios in the cordon tables.

    The interval between shake and surge is scheduled labor: battening crews walk the line, soft stores move off exposed faces, and vents open in the order the wave will arrive. Seal work follows the tables' cool windows, and inspectors retest every seal the surge touched. Cordon training records dated false passes in which a pre-surge inspection was trusted afterward. In the central reach, overlapping events keep the ground warm year-round. A long warm week after a resonance storm suspends scheduled seal work until the tables show the ground returning to its working range.
  PROSE

  cue "Six hours after the shake the survey strips along the line darken one after another, the rail grows warm under still air, and the battening crew ahead of the wave works with the unhurried speed of practice against a posted schedule."
  cue "The inspector's chalk crosses out yesterday's pass marks along the touched reach — every seal the wave met is unpassed until proven again — and the crew behind her starts the second round."
  affordance "The cordon tables turn the surge into working time — the event-to-surge interval is a posted schedule for battening, venting, and moving stores, and the surge itself re-anneals glass and reveals every weak seal while the crews are there to catch it."
  pressure "The surge can soften a seal that passed before it arrived, so crews move soft stores during the posted interval and retest every touched seal after the wave."
  variation "Discrete events give single surges the tables predict closely; resonance storms give the long warm week and a general stand-down; the central reach rings warm year-round and its crews work afterheat as climate."
  variation "Gap households read the survey strips on their own door frames and batten by them, and the cordon's children learn event-hour arithmetic as a household chore before they learn it as physics."
end
